WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:06.000
The tree describes placement relationships, while the skyline determines the height where each block lands.

2
00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:12.138
First place root A at the origin, then process its entire left subtree.

3
00:00:13.228 --> 00:00:20.700
A left child starts at its parent’s right edge; B, C, and E land before D is processed.

4
00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:28.710
In the reference tree, the highest skyline under D is A’s top, so D lands at height two.

5
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.776
If we swap the names A and C, will D still land at height two?

6
00:00:36.516 --> 00:00:43.388
Watch the swapped layout; D reaches over taller B, which lifts it to height three.

7
00:00:44.478 --> 00:00:51.110
The box grows from twenty-seven to thirty-six; legality alone does not say whether the swap improved it.

8
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:59.384
Edit the tree in the lab, and explain heights using the skyline rather than memorizing child labels.
